Spec: Independent Android SDK relay acceptance

Purpose:
  Verify real private Binder descriptors and application bytes through the server-authorized FRP backend.

Owns:
  ./FrpConsumerTest.java

Must:
  Use only the public signature-pinned SDK from a distinct installed UID and signer; never invoke Agent internals.
  Negotiate relay separately, require local owner approval and preserve exact retained path across polling and close.
  Verify a sixty-four MiB hash, request half-close and one-use attachment, and keep two simultaneous same-application streams during active local and server revocation.
  Bound every wait and expose only aggregate test results in target-private files.

  Close one of two shared-runtime streams through the public SDK and prove the other remains ready with a live blocked read.

  A new open after server grant revocation returns a fixed authorization failure without reaching the business server.

  Exercise the admitted-budget planner through the public direct-only SDK method over an authenticated reachable IPv4 candidate and record LAN evidence separately from XTCP.
  Declare the fixture relay import with an explicit zero direct window so formal relay acceptance is deterministic while preserving the experimental relay scenario.
